# SVGs are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists: scripts/logo-manifest.mjs records each logo's
# working-tree size as `bytes` in src/data/logoLibrary.json. With
# core.autocrlf=true, Windows checks an SVG out with CRLF, so its size is
# larger than on a machine that checks out LF — one measured example is
# 8884 bytes on Windows against an 8834-byte blob, a 50-byte gap.
#
# That costs twice:
#   1. logoLibrary.json shows ~1180 changed lines of nothing after any
#      cross-machine checkout, which is enough noise to hide real work.
#   2. `bytes` is the cache key for the measured `tone` field, so every
#      entry misses and toneOf() re-measures the brightness of all 1106
#      logos from scratch.
#
# Pinning LF makes the size identical everywhere, so both go away.
*.svg text eol=lf

# The manifest the script above writes. It is generated with LF on every
# platform, so pinning the checkout to LF stops it round-tripping between
# CRLF on disk and LF from the generator on each predev/prebuild run.
src/data/logoLibrary.json text eol=lf

# Raster and font assets are never line-ending converted. Git's auto-detection
# already gets this right; stating it means a future *.xyz rule cannot widen
# into them by accident.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
